  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "note_66",
      "text": "Reports summary statistics for each wired column, one row per variable: n, mean, median, standard deviation, the standard error of the mean (SD / sqrt(n)) and the 95% confidence interval of the mean (mean ± t(0.975, n - 1) × SEM, Student 1908; it assumes the mean is roughly normal, so treat it with care for small, skewed samples), min, max, range, first and third quartiles, IQR, skewness and (excess) kurtosis. Skewness and kurtosis use the bias-corrected sample formulae (matching scipy). Quick-plot draws a histogram of each column so you can see the distribution behind the numbers.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 24,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 190
    }
